Sweller

Sweller is an educational agent inspired by Cognitive Load Theory and the Get the Gist strategy.

The goal is simple: help students understand difficult topics without overwhelming them with information.

Instead of immediately generating the largest possible answer, Sweller tries to:

identify the core idea of a topic
detect missing prerequisites
reduce unnecessary cognitive load
build small learning paths
verify understanding before moving forward
Architecture
Skills define learning behaviors such as gist extraction, prerequisite detection, study planning, and understanding checks.
Tools provide structured educational logic, including knowledge estimation and learning path generation.
Lib contains reusable learning models and cognition-related utilities.
Evals are used to measure whether the agent behaves as expected.